  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The electric field associated with an electromagnetic wave propagating in a dielectric medium is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>14</mn></msup><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp;Which of the following option(s) is(are) correct?</p><p>[Given: The speed of light in vacuum, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Ojp7M",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mi>sin</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi>Wb</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1IJyr",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mi>sin</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>14</mn></msup><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi>Wb</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hrnTM",
      "text": "The wave is polarized in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>-plane with polarization angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math> with respect to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
